      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We experienced 2 patients in whom conventional percutaneous methods were not useful for acute occlusions sequel to coronary angioplasty. Acute occlusions seemed to be caused by large dissections. Pulling an inflated balloon at the dissected lesions achieved reentry from the false lumen to the true lumen, thus resolving collapse of the true lumen and recanalizing the occluded coronary artery."},
